From: Stanislav Gabenov <gabenovstan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: Octeon: add DAP-2690 PCI interrupt routing

The DAP-2690 A1 wires slot 2 INTA to PCI INT1 and slot 3 INTA to
PCI INT0.  The CN3005_EVB_HS5 fallback maps those two slots in the
opposite order, causing ath9k to receive only unhandled interrupts and
the kernel to disable both IRQs.

The vendor kernel confirms the board routing as slot 2 -> CVMX IRQ 45
(PCI INT1) and slot 3 -> CVMX IRQ 44 (PCI INT0).

Signed-off-by: Stanislav Gabenov <gabenovstan@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/mips/pci/pci-octeon.c
+++ b/arch/mips/pci/pci-octeon.c
@@ -195,6 +195,8 @@ const char *octeon_get_pci_interrupts(vo
 	 */
 	if (of_machine_is_compatible("dlink,dsr-500n"))
 		return "CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC";
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("dlink,dap-2690-a1"))
+		return "AABAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA";
 	switch (octeon_bootinfo->board_type) {
 	case CVMX_BOARD_TYPE_NAO38:
 		/* This is really the NAC38 */
